{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nResidual non-code capacity-measurement work split from `witted-invisible-roan` after the serving-path fix landed.\n\nParent residual AC: the measurement campaign has produced the numbers the OOM decision needs — peak MCP RSS during a gate, steady-state RSS per container, and how RSS scales with ticket size.\n\nCurrent operator ruling: run the measurement now if it does not require pausing parallel sessions. If it would require pausing them, defer and report. This ticket is an operational evidence campaign, not a code change.\n\n## Plan\n1. Confirm whether the measurement can run with only existing host/CloudWatch data and read-only live probes. Do not pause or stop parallel sessions.\n2. Collect steady-state per-container RSS from live `docker stats --no-stream` and CloudWatch `rebar/host:container_memory_rss_bytes` for the current window.\n3. Collect peak MCP/gate RSS from existing `GATE_PEAK_RSS` markers and container metrics for recent gate windows. Do not start artificial load that competes with active sessions.\n4. Derive the RSS-vs-ticket-size/capacity conclusion from recorded gate samples and ticket-store sizing data already captured in the parent/children. If live data cannot answer that without a quiet/load window, record the exact deferred measurement.\n5. Post commands, timestamps, source windows, measured values, caveats, and follow-up links as ticket comments.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Comment records peak MCP/gate RSS values with source command/log query and timestamp window.\n- [x] Comment records steady-state per-container RSS values with source command/log query and timestamp window.\n- [x] Comment records an RSS-vs-ticket-size/capacity conclusion, or records the exact remaining load/quiet-window measurement that cannot run without pausing parallel sessions.\n- [x] Comment records whether the campaign completed now or was deferred by the no-pause constraint.\n- [x] Follow-up implementation/design tickets are linked if the measurements expose new work.\n\n## Verification\n- Read-only host/CloudWatch/log commands are included in the evidence comment.\n- No code files are modified for this ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789044938168203001,"uuid":"c5d4180d-6a41-4145-ba4a-61f8687375a4"}